NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - ONE INSTANCE FOR THE DAY: the family runs one instance 00:00-15:58 ET; the open layer's w_start / w_end clip the entries to decisions at the 10:00 .. 15:15 closes; the cap of 2 is a DAY cap and one position at a time holds all day. The passes only name the clock for the random control and the reads. (The lane's generic one-instance note says 'entries 10:30-15:30'; this family's own window is 00:00-15:58 and the sheet's w_start / w_end make it 10:00-15:30.)
  - THE AUTOCORRELATION FILTER of the video (AC <= -0.1, the 'dip') is switched off on purpose (one filter).
  - THE STOP: 2 x the simple mean of the last 20 true ranges of the 15-minute bars, frozen at the signal bar (early in the day this window still holds pre-market bars, so stops are smaller then); the video's trailing stop is off.
  - THE INDICATORS restart at 00:00 ET and need 26 bars (06:30 ET) before any value.
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, $4 a round turn, tick replay, 1 NQ).
  - FLAT: every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - THE TEST DAYS (2025-07-01 on) ARE NOT READ by this sheet: build days only (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30); the 3:1 block walk-forward is a separate, pre-registered read (hunt PREREG Gate 2).

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - ONE INSTANCE FOR THE DAY (asia, london, pre, nyam, mid, pm are one window, entries 10:30-15:30, flat 15:58): the cap of 2 trades is a DAY cap, one position at a time holds for the whole day, and the family's loss stop counts over the day (none). The random control and the reads still go pass by pass (nyam, mid, pm), matched by day.
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).
  - The stop is the family's structure level of each entry (its size differs from trade to trade; the engine never puts it closer than two ticks or 0.25 ATR); `stop_val` is not used.

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
